  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.9">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 2.9</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.9" corresp="#wit-q">Preter discarcatam lanam et dissutum unctum et tres porcos uiuos licebat eis emere in naues suas.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="2.9" corresp="#wit-q">Praeter discarcatam lanam et dissutum unctum, et tres porcos vivos licebat eis emere in naves suas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">Besides wool, which had been unloaded, and melted fat, they were also permitted to buy three live pigs for their ships.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Ausser ausgeladener Wolle und zerlassenem Fett durften sie auch drei lebendige Schweine auf ihre Schiffe hin einkaufen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Besides unloaded wool and rendered fat, they were also allowed to buy three live pigs [to take] onto their ships.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Thorpe corrects ‘dissutum’ to ‘dissolutum’.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
